// src/schema_wire.pdx — cat.SCHEMA-001 (cat#27, Wave L / v1.2.1-A)
// SchemaWire module: registers RawByteChunk@0.1's canonical DDL hash
// with libpdx-schema-registry and caches the returned schema id.
//
// Why this is a local stand-in, not a real libpdx-schema-registry link
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// `libpdx-schema-registry` (github.com/paideia-os/libpdx-schema-registry)
// is confirmed INERT at this writing per paideia-os#2000 ("R90-XREPO.006
// Stand up libpdx-schema-registry service"): the service broker only
// knows two hardcoded test names (svc.foo/svc.foobar) and no real
// registry client library is adopted anywhere in the tools tree (`grep
// libpdx-schema-registry` across the org's satellite repos returns only
// design-doc references and two prior sibling-repo fallback landings --
// mount.pdxfs's and mkfs.pdxfs's own src/pipe_wire.pdx -- neither of
// which links a real client either). cat's own deps.list carries a
// single dependency (`libpdx-argv >= 1.1.3`); no schema-registry client
// crate exists to link against.
//
// A true weak-symbol default (STB_WEAK, resolved to a fallback body only
// when no stronger definition is linked) is also not an option: per
// libpdx-argv's own version_backend.pdx header ("the paideia-as 0.36
// encoder does not currently expose the STB_WEAK binding"), this
// toolchain has no linker-weak mechanism to fall back on. Emitting an
// `extern`/UND reference to a symbol no object in this build provides
// would fail `ld -nostdlib --fatal-warnings` outright (tools/build.sh
// links every src/*.pdx object into one flat cat.elf).
//
// This file therefore takes the same shape as the mount.pdxfs / mkfs.
// pdxfs precedent: `libpdx_schema_registry_register` is defined IN this
// module as a real, linkable function carrying the eventual real
// contract's argument shape (a DDL-hash pointer in), but its BODY is a
// placeholder that unconditionally returns CAT_SCHEMA_ID_PLACEHOLDER
// (0xE05A_C000) without inspecting the pointer. This is the "WEAK stub"
// the issue asks for, expressed the only way this toolchain supports it:
// a real symbol, real linkage, placeholder behaviour, one documented
// call site (`schema_wire_register`, invoked once from src/entry.pdx's
// entry_done tail) that is the ONLY thing that needs to change when a
// real libpdx-schema-registry client lands -- the function keeps its
// signature, only its body swaps from "return placeholder" to "resolve
// via the real client and return the registry's schema id".
//
// Record consumed
// ----------------
// RawByteChunk@0.1's canonical DDL hash lives at
// `RawByteChunk::_rbc_schema_hash` (src/raw_byte_chunk.pdx, cat.ENH-008 /
// #21) -- a 32-byte SHA-256 fingerprint of the canonical
// "RawByteChunk@0.1\noffset:u64\nbytes:[u8]\n" DDL text. This module
// passes its address (not its bytes) to libpdx_schema_registry_register,
// matching the eventual real contract's expected argument shape (a
// pointer the real client would hash-lookup / register against, not a
// copy).
//
// cat_schema_id is consumed by src/pipe_emit.pdx (cat#29) as the
// `schema_id` field of every CatPipeRecord@0.1 emission -- the two
// issues share this one integration point deliberately: the semantic-
// pipe record annotates itself with whatever schema-registry id this
// run resolved (0xE05A_C000 today; a real registry-assigned id once
// SCHEMA-001's other half lands).
//
// paideia-as compliance
// ----------------------
//   - Module name PascalCase basename (`SchemaWire`).
//   - No `test` mnemonic; no zero-checks in this file at all.
//   - No `and rN, imm64` on r8-r15 (no ANDs anywhere in this file).
//   - No 2-op `imul r, imm` (no multiplies in this file).
//   - No `neg` mnemonic.
//   - No byte-register aliases; no byte loads/stores in this file at
//     all (both functions move whole 8-byte pointers/ids).
//   - No `qword ptr` / `dword ptr` Intel-style sizing -- plain
//     `mov [mem], reg` for the one 8-byte store.
//   - Reserved-label discipline: neither function branches, so no
//     label prefix is required.
//   - `r11` reserved as `lea` scratch, reloaded immediately before the
//     one `.bss` store it guards.
//   - `libpdx_schema_registry_register` is a two-instruction leaf
//     (`mov rax, imm; ret`) with no stack use and no nested calls, so
//     the caller's rsp alignment at its own call site is functionally
//     immaterial to it; `schema_wire_register` nonetheless brackets
//     that call with `sub rsp, 8` / `add rsp, 8` to keep the project's
//     rsp%16==0-at-CALL convention intact transitively (entry rsp%16==8
//     is the universal post-CALL SysV state this module's own caller,
//     src/entry.pdx's entry_done, delivers).

module SchemaWire = structure {

  // ============================================================================
  // CAT_SCHEMA_ID_PLACEHOLDER — the id `libpdx_schema_registry_register`
  // returns unconditionally until a real libpdx-schema-registry client
  // is adopted. Chosen to read unambiguously as a cat-owned sentinel
  // (0xE05A_C000 -- "E05A" evokes "cat" loosely as a hex mnemonic slot
  // reserved for this tool, "C000" marks it a Cat-family placeholder
  // Id) rather than 0, which would be indistinguishable from
  // cat_schema_id's own zero-initialised default and could silently
  // read as "never registered" to a downstream consumer.
  // ============================================================================
  pub let CAT_SCHEMA_ID_PLACEHOLDER : u64 = 0xE05AC000

  // ============================================================================
  // cat_schema_id — cached result of the last schema_wire_register()
  // call. Zero until the first call; consumers (src/pipe_emit.pdx)
  // treat 0 as "not yet registered" and CAT_SCHEMA_ID_PLACEHOLDER as
  // "registered against the placeholder registry stand-in".
  // ============================================================================
  pub let mut cat_schema_id : u64 = 0

  // ============================================================================
  // libpdx_schema_registry_register(ddl_hash_ptr) -> schema_id
  //
  // Signature: libpdx_schema_registry_register : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{}
  //   RDI (input):  ddl_hash_ptr — pointer to a 32-byte schema DDL
  //                 fingerprint (e.g. RawByteChunk::_rbc_schema_hash).
  //                 Accepted per the eventual real contract's shape;
  //                 UNUSED by this placeholder body — the real client
  //                 will hash-lookup / register using these bytes.
  //   RAX (output): CAT_SCHEMA_ID_PLACEHOLDER, unconditionally.
  //
  // See module header: this is the toolchain-shaped substitute for a
  // true STB_WEAK default (unavailable in paideia-as 0.36). Real leaf,
  // no stack use, no nested calls -- rsp alignment at its own call
  // site is immaterial (see module header note).
  // ============================================================================
  pub let libpdx_schema_registry_register : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (ddl_hash_ptr: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {},
      capabilities: {},
      justification: "cat.SCHEMA-001 (cat#27) libpdx_schema_registry_register placeholder. Real libpdx-schema-registry client is not adopted anywhere in the tools tree (paideia-os#2000 -- the service broker is inert) and paideia-as 0.36 has no STB_WEAK linkage to fall back to (per libpdx-argv version_backend.pdx's own header note), so this function IS the fallback: a real, linkable symbol with the eventual real contract's argument shape (ddl_hash_ptr in rdi) whose body unconditionally returns CAT_SCHEMA_ID_PLACEHOLDER (0xE05AC000) without touching rdi. Two-instruction leaf: mov rax, imm32; ret. No effects, no capabilities -- pure computation. When a real client lands this function's body is the ONLY thing that changes (resolve via the real client, return its schema id); the signature and every call site stay identical.",
      block: {
        mov rax, 0xE05AC000;         // CAT_SCHEMA_ID_PLACEHOLDER
        ret;
      }
    }

  // ============================================================================
  // schema_wire_register() -> ()
  //
  // Signature: schema_wire_register : () -> () !{mem} @{}
  //
  // Calls libpdx_schema_registry_register with RawByteChunk@0.1's
  // canonical DDL-hash pointer and stores the result into
  // cat_schema_id. Called once from src/entry.pdx's entry_done tail,
  // immediately before the pipe_emit_send call that reads
  // cat_schema_id back out (cat#29).
  //
  // Register plan: no callee-save touched; rdi carries the hash
  // pointer into the nested call, rax carries its return back out to
  // the `.bss` store. Entry rsp%16==8 (post-CALL SysV state, the
  // universal condition for any function invoked via `call` from a
  // caller that was itself aligned to 0). `sub rsp, 8` / `add rsp, 8`
  // bracket the nested call to land rsp%16==0 at that CALL site,
  // matching the project's alignment convention (see module header —
  // functionally immaterial for THIS particular callee, kept anyway
  // for consistency and because a future real client body may not
  // stay stack-free).
  // ============================================================================
  pub let schema_wire_register : () -> () !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem},
      capabilities: {},
      justification: "cat.SCHEMA-001 (cat#27) schema_wire_register. Sequence: (1) sub rsp, 8 -- align for the nested call (entry rsp%16==8 post-CALL SysV state; -8 yields 0). (2) lea rdi, [rip + _rbc_schema_hash] -- address of RawByteChunk@0.1's canonical DDL-hash fingerprint (RawByteChunk module, src/raw_byte_chunk.pdx, cat.ENH-008 / #21), passed by pointer per the eventual real registry contract's shape. (3) call libpdx_schema_registry_register -- rax = schema id (CAT_SCHEMA_ID_PLACEHOLDER today). (4) lea r11, [rip + cat_schema_id]; mov [r11], rax -- persist the result. (5) add rsp, 8 -- restore (this function returns normally to src/entry.pdx's entry_done, unlike _start's @no_frame posture, so the stack must balance before ret). No test mnemonic, no and/imul/neg, no byte ops. r11 reloaded immediately before its one use per the project's r11-scratch convention.",
      block: {
        sub rsp, 8;
        lea rdi, [rip + _rbc_schema_hash];
        call libpdx_schema_registry_register;
        lea r11, [rip + cat_schema_id];
        mov [r11], rax;
        add rsp, 8;
        ret;
      }
    }
}
